# Project Memory – LinkedIn Clone

> Full-stack LinkedIn-style social network. Real-time via Socket.IO. AI via Anthropic Claude. Dark/light theme.

## Stack Snapshot

| Layer | Tech |
|---|---|
| Runtime | Node.js + Express 5, ES Modules (`"type":"module"`) |
| DB | MongoDB + Mongoose 8 (db name: `linkedin`) |
| Auth | JWT 7d TTL · bcryptjs · cookie + Bearer |
| Real-time | Socket.IO 4 |
| AI | `@anthropic-ai/sdk` (Anthropic Claude) |
| Storage | Cloudinary (multer → temp disk → upload → delete) |
| Frontend | React 19 + Vite 7 |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`, class-based dark mode) |
| Routing | React Router DOM v7 |
| HTTP | Axios via `frontend/api/apiHelper.js` (interceptors, auto-token) |

## Ports & URLs

| | Value |
|---|---|
| Backend | `http://localhost:8020` |
| Frontend | `http://localhost:5173` |
| Socket origin | `VITE_BACKEND_API_URL` minus `/api` |
| API base env | `VITE_BACKEND_API_URL` (e.g. `http://localhost:8020/api`) |

## Data Models (key fields)

**User** – `firstName lastName userName(unique,lc) email(unique,lc) password profileImage coverImage headline skills[] education[{college,degree,fieldOfStudy}] experience[{title,company,description}] location gender connection[User] accessToken`

**Post** – `author(User) description image like[User] comment[{content, user(User)}]`

**Connection** – `sender(User) receiver(User) status(pending|accepted|rejected)`

**Notification** – `receiver(User) type(like|comment|connectionAccepted) relatedUser(User) relatedPost(Post)`

## API Route Map

```
POST  /api/auth/signup                  – register
POST  /api/auth/login                   – login → JWT cookie + token body
GET   /api/auth/logout                  – clear cookie

GET   /api/user/get-current-user        – auth: req.user._id
PUT   /api/user/update-profile          – multipart: profileImage, coverImage
GET   /api/user/profile/:userName
GET   /api/user/search?query=
GET   /api/user/suggest-users

POST  /api/post/create-post             – multipart: description, image
GET   /api/post/get-all-posts
GET   /api/post/like/:id                – toggle like
POST  /api/post/comment/:id             – body: { content }
POST  /api/post/suggest-posts           – body: { aiPrompt } → AI-drafted post
GET   /api/post/suggest-comment/:id    – AI comment (saves + emits socket)

POST  /api/connection/send/:id
PUT   /api/connection/accept/:connectionId
PUT   /api/connection/reject/:connectionId
GET   /api/connection/get-status/:userId  → "connect"|"pending"|"received"|"disconnect"
DELETE /api/connection/remove/:userId
GET   /api/connection/requests
GET   /api/connection/

GET   /api/notification/               – fetch notifications
```

## Socket Event Map

| Emitter | Event | Payload |
|---|---|---|
| Client→Server | `register` | `userId` |
| Client→Server | `chat-message` | `{ message, intent }` |
| Server→Client | `bot-reply` | `{ content }` |
| Server→Client | `likeUpdated` | `{ postId, likes }` (broadcast) |
| Server→Client | `commentAdded` | `{ postId, comm }` (broadcast) |
| Server→Client | `statusUpdate` | `{ updatedUserId, newStatus }` (targeted) |

`newStatus` values: `"connect"` `"pending"` `"received"` `"disconnect"`

## Auth Flow (compressed)

1. Login → backend sets cookie `token` + returns `{ user, token }` in body
2. Frontend: `localStorage.setItem("token", token)` + sets `AuthContext.user`
3. `apiHelpers` request interceptor injects `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every request
4. `isAuth` middleware: checks `req.cookies.token` first, then `Authorization` header → sets `req.userId` + `req.user`
5. On app load: `AuthProvider` reads `localStorage.token` → calls `/user/get-current-user` → restores state
6. Logout: clear `localStorage`, set user `null`, redirect `/login`

